      "content": "The argument that these giants are simply \"better\" ignores how their size is used to crush competitors before they can even launch, rather than just winning through superior products. Breaking them up is not about killing innovation; it is about dismantling the artificial barriers that prevent new, disruptive startups from challenging the status quo. If we let these monopolies remain unchecked, we risk a future where only the biggest corporations survive, and the market becomes stagnant rather than dynamic.",
